# Notebook diffs.
#
# Re-running a notebook rewrites its whole JSON, so a one-cell change shows up as
# a multi-megabyte blob and review becomes impossible. nbdime diffs by cell
# instead, and it does this without stripping outputs: the charts stay committed,
# because they are what makes a notebook readable on GitHub and they cannot be
# regenerated from a clone (the store the notebooks read is not in the repo).
#
# Enable once per clone:  pip install nbdime && nbdime config-git --enable
*.ipynb diff=jupyternotebook
*.ipynb merge=jupyternotebook

# Re-exported SVG panels are coordinate soup: a cosmetic re-run rewrites every
# path, which buries real changes. Collapse them in review.
research/poster/assets/*.svg -diff

# The metric JSONs are the opposite. They are small, and they hold the numbers
# printed on the board, so their diff is the single most reviewable thing here:
# it shows exactly which headline figure moved. Keep them diffable.

# Keep GitHub's language stats about the library, not the research exports.
research/poster/assets/* linguist-vendored=true
